WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:03.739
Let's go next to, where do we want to go?

00:00:03.739 --> 00:00:07.689
Let's go to our caller from the nine to five
area code.

00:00:07.689 --> 00:00:09.910
Who's calling today from nine to five.

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:11.390
Hi, Zoe.

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:13.620
Yeah, that's you.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.110
Hi David.

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:18.310
I'm a huge fan of the show.

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:21.919
Um, I just wanted to ask you about again,
the impeachment process.

00:00:21.919 --> 00:00:25.749
Um, right now, you know, with the release
of the transcripts, there seems to be clearly

00:00:25.749 --> 00:00:27.349
enough evidence for impeachment.

00:00:27.349 --> 00:00:32.320
But the vibe I'm getting from Republicans
is they see this as an absolute win.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:34.800
They know that impeachment has like horrible
poor rating, I think.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.300
I think it's around 30%.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.600
I'm not sure.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.120
And they think it'll help them in 2020.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.120
Yeah.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.940
It seems that both sides are assuming this
is a win for them and it seems that there's

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:46.100
going to be one clear winner and loser.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:51.489
Um, um, I'm just going to ask like based on
this, do you see this as hurting the Democrats

00:00:51.489 --> 00:00:52.960
in 2020 or helping them

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.679
it, so my commentary this week has been that
it depends on what actually happens and it's

00:00:57.679 --> 00:00:59.110
basically three different things.

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:04.839
Number one, what information that was previously
unknown to the general public is revealed

00:01:04.839 --> 00:01:06.720
through the impeachment inquiry process.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:07.890
That's question number one.

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:15.030
Question number two, does Donald Trump successfully
turn himself into the victim martyr?

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:19.230
Whatever phrase you want to use, because that
would absolutely embolden Trump.

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:21.580
And then the other thing I think is important,
I don't know where you're getting the number

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:24.610
that only 30% of Americans are in favor of
impeachment.

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:28.340
Last I looked more than half of the country
was in favor of an impeachment inquiry.

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:31.070
I don't, I've not seen any evidence to suggest
that's changed.

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:32.070
Oh, okay.

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:33.070
Okay.

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:34.070
I didn't know that.

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:37.469
Um, yeah, I mean that was, that was my question.

00:01:37.469 --> 00:01:38.469
Thank you.

00:01:38.469 --> 00:01:42.080
I'm curious about where did you get that 30%
of the country supports impeachment?

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:45.280
Um, I got it from, um, the Hill.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:49.430
They just, uh, re put out a video today about
it, I think, and they mentioned it's around

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:50.970
30 to 35% I think.

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:51.970
Okay.

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:52.970
I'll check that out.

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:53.970
Yeah.

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:55.040
The polls I had seen revoked above 50%.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.040
Okay.

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.040
Okay.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:58.040
Yeah.

00:01:58.040 --> 00:01:59.040
Alright, thank you.

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:00.040
Okay.

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:01.040
Thank you for the call.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:01.043
I appreciate it.

